    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n14492" root="ربض" body-key="r">
    
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">رُبْضَةٌ</span></b> , applied to a man, <i>i q.</i> ↓ <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مُتَرَبِّضٌ</span></b> ; (K;)
i. e. (tropical:)  <i>Remaining stationary, and impotent;</i> (TA;)
as also ↓ <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">رُبَضَةٌ</span></b> . (K.) ＝   
    <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer1"> </span>-A2-  See also <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">رِبْضَةٌ</span>. ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b2-  Also
(assumed tropical:)  <i>A portion,</i> (K,) or <i>large portion,</i> (IDrd,) <i>of</i>
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">ثَرِيد</span> [i. e. <i>crumbled bread moistened with broth</i>].
(IDrd, K.) ＝   
    <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer1"> </span>-A3-  See also <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">رُبْصَةٌ</span>, with the unpointed <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">ص</span>.

